From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0016] parser: recover orphan DSML invokes from inside
 <think> too, not just from CONTENT

WHAT BREAKS. `0009`'s orphan-invoke recovery (port of vllm-project/vllm#49117)
only wires the (CONTENT, INVOKE_PREFIX) and (CONTENT, FOREIGN_START)
transitions. DeepSeek-V4-0731 defaults to starting every turn already in
REASONING state -- no explicit opening `<think>` tag, per `0008`'s
"omitted thinking/enable_thinking means thinking=True" default, which
just flips the *default* of a thinking->initial_state mapping that
already existed upstream before `0008` touched it. So on this tree, and
on any stock vLLM + #49117 caller that explicitly passes `thinking=True`
(a normal, documented way to call this parser -- nothing fork-specific),
an orphan invoke emitted before `</think>` never reaches CONTENT at all.
The whole block -- and, in the non-streaming path, everything scanned
after it -- gets folded into REASONING_CHUNK and is either lost or
surfaces as raw DSML text, which is exactly the garbled
`</parameter></｜DSML｜parameter></｜DSML｜invoke></｜DSML｜tool_calls>`
leak this patch was written to reproduce and fix.

CONFIRMED VIA THE PORTED PR #49117 TEST SUITE. Applying that suite's own
tests (`tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v4.py`) against this tree,
`TestMissingToolStart`/`TestOrphanInvokeNameValidation` fail wholesale
(38/41) -- not because recovery is subtly wrong, but because every test
in that suite constructs `DeepSeekV4Parser(mock_tokenizer, tools=[...])`
without pinning `thinking`, which upstream defaults to CONTENT-initial
but `0008` defaults to REASONING-initial on this tree. Tracing a single
case (`tests/parser/engine/parser_engine.py:_on_terminal`) confirms the
INVOKE_PREFIX terminal is scanned correctly but has no
`(REASONING, "INVOKE_PREFIX")` entry in the transition table, so it falls
through to plain REASONING_CHUNK content. Forcing `thinking=False`
confirms the CONTENT-state path itself is unaffected -- this is purely a
missing REASONING-state mirror, not a regression in `0009`.

THE FIX. Add `(REASONING, "INVOKE_PREFIX")` and `(REASONING,
"FOREIGN_START")` transitions mirroring `0009`'s CONTENT-state ones
exactly, additionally emitting `REASONING_END` (matching the existing
`(REASONING, "TOOL_START")` transition's pattern for the wrapped-call
case). Purely additive -- CONTENT-state behavior is untouched.

Also adds a REASONING-state regression suite
(`TestReasoningStateOrphanInvoke`) covering non-streaming, streaming
char-by-char, the true production default (no `thinking` kwarg at all),
and the undeclared-name guard, mirroring the existing CONTENT-state
coverage from `0009`/the gist series (`0010`-`0015`).

UPSTREAM. This gap is in vllm-project/vllm#49117 itself, not introduced
by combining our patches -- rasatpetabit's gist (`0010`-`0015`) is built
directly on #49117's baseline with zero fuzz, so it inherits the same
gap. Worth reporting upstream on #49117 independent of this port.
--- a/vllm/parser/deepseek_v4.py
+++ b/vllm/parser/deepseek_v4.py
@@ -191,6 +191,20 @@
                 ParserState.FOREIGN_BLOCK,
                 (EventType.TEXT_CHUNK,),
             ),
+            # Same recovery, reached while still inside <think>: DSv4-0731
+            # defaults to starting a turn already in REASONING state (no
+            # explicit opening tag), so an orphan invoke emitted before
+            # </think> never reaches CONTENT at all and must be handled
+            # here too, not just from CONTENT.
+            (ParserState.REASONING, "INVOKE_PREFIX"): Transition(
+                ParserState.TOOL_NAME,
+                (EventType.REASONING_END, EventType.TOOL_CALL_START),
+                validate_tool_name=True,
+            ),
+            (ParserState.REASONING, "FOREIGN_START"): Transition(
+                ParserState.FOREIGN_BLOCK,
+                (EventType.REASONING_END, EventType.TEXT_CHUNK),
+            ),
             (ParserState.FOREIGN_BLOCK, "FOREIGN_END"): Transition(
                 ParserState.CONTENT,
                 (EventType.TEXT_CHUNK,),
--- a/tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v4.py
+++ b/tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v4.py
@@ -1769,3 +1769,89 @@
         assert eos_text not in output.reasoning
         assert output.content == ""
         assert output.tool_calls == []
+
+
+# ── Orphan invoke recovered from inside REASONING, not just CONTENT ─────
+
+
+class TestReasoningStateOrphanInvoke:
+    """Orphan invoke recovery must also work while still inside <think>.
+
+    DeepSeek-V4-0731 defaults to starting a turn already in REASONING
+    state (no explicit opening tag -- see the ``thinking`` default in
+    ``DeepSeekV4Parser.__init__``), so a request that never sees an
+    explicit ``thinking=False`` runs the recovery path introduced for
+    TestMissingToolStart / TestOrphanInvokeNameValidation from REASONING,
+    not CONTENT. Those tests all construct the parser without pinning
+    ``thinking``, so on this tree they exercise REASONING already; this
+    class pins it explicitly so the intent is not accidental, and adds
+    the streaming char-by-char case those already cover for CONTENT.
+    """
+
+    @pytest.fixture
+    def weather_tool(self):
+        return _make_tool("get_weather", {"location": {"type": "string"}})
+
+    def _reasoning_parser(self, mock_tokenizer, mock_request, *tools):
+        parser = DeepSeekV4Parser(
+            mock_tokenizer,
+            tools=list(tools),
+            chat_template_kwargs={"thinking": True},
+        )
+        mock_request.tools = list(tools)
+        mock_request.tool_choice = None
+        return parser
+
+    def test_non_streaming_orphan_invoke_from_reasoning(
+        self, mock_tokenizer, mock_request, weather_tool
+    ):
+        parser = self._reasoning_parser(mock_tokenizer, mock_request, weather_tool)
+        text = _invoke("get_weather", ("location", "true", "NYC")) + DSML_TOOL_END
+        result = parser.extract_tool_calls(text, mock_request)
+
+        assert result.tools_called is True
+        assert len(result.tool_calls) == 1
+        assert result.tool_calls[0].function.name == "get_weather"
+        args = json.loads(result.tool_calls[0].function.arguments)
+        assert args == {"location": "NYC"}
+
+    def test_default_thinking_matches_explicit_reasoning(
+        self, mock_tokenizer, mock_request, weather_tool
+    ):
+        """No ``thinking`` kwarg at all must behave the same as pinning it,
+        since that is the real request shape in production."""
+        parser = DeepSeekV4Parser(mock_tokenizer, tools=[weather_tool])
+        mock_request.tools = [weather_tool]
+        mock_request.tool_choice = None
+        text = _invoke("get_weather", ("location", "true", "NYC")) + DSML_TOOL_END
+
+        result = parser.extract_tool_calls(text, mock_request)
+
+        assert result.tools_called is True
+        assert len(result.tool_calls) == 1
+
+    def test_streaming_orphan_invoke_char_by_char_from_reasoning(
+        self, mock_tokenizer, mock_request, weather_tool
+    ):
+        parser = self._reasoning_parser(mock_tokenizer, mock_request, weather_tool)
+        text = _invoke("get_weather", ("location", "true", "NYC")) + DSML_TOOL_END
+        results = simulate_tool_streaming(parser, mock_request, list(text))
+
+        assert collect_function_name(results) == "get_weather"
+        args = collect_tool_arguments(results)
+        assert json.loads(args) == {"location": "NYC"}
+
+    def test_undeclared_name_stays_reasoning_content(
+        self, mock_tokenizer, mock_request, weather_tool
+    ):
+        """Prose quoting the marker inside <think> for an undeclared tool
+        must not be recovered as a call, mirroring the CONTENT-state
+        guard from TestOrphanInvokeNameValidation."""
+        parser = self._reasoning_parser(mock_tokenizer, mock_request, weather_tool)
+        text = (
+            _invoke("get_nothing", ("location", "true", "NYC"))
+            + DSML_THINK_END
+        )
+        result = parser.extract_tool_calls(text, mock_request)
+
+        assert result.tools_called is False
